  "answer": "",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Write x and y with the definition of odd, using two different new letters.",
    "Expand the product: every term except one has a factor of 2."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $x$ and $y$ are odd, $x = 2a + 1$ and $y = 2b + 1$ for some integers $a, b$.",
    "$xy = (2a+1)(2b+1) = 4ab + 2a + 2b + 1 = 2(2ab + a + b) + 1$.",
    "$2ab + a + b$ is an integer, so $xy$ is odd. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "hammack-bop3",
    "section": "Chapter 4 exercises, #4 (p. 126)",
    "note": "This exact exercise, restated in ProofLab's words. Uses Definition 4.2 (odd)."
  },
